---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Cojiro Quiz is an unofficial, crowdsourced answer key for the Ocarina of Time companion app quizzes. How it works and how to contribute."
>
  <div class="wrap narrow prose">
    <h1>About Cojiro Quiz</h1>
    <p>
      Cojiro Quiz is a searchable answer key for the quizzes in the Ocarina of Time companion app. The quiz is timed,
      so the site is built to be quick: type a word or two from the question and the answer is right there.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every question comes from players. Questions are stored exactly as the app shows them, in whatever language they
      were shown in, and are never translated.
    </p>

    <h2>How to contribute</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Take a screenshot of a quiz question. The result screen (after you answer) is best, because it shows which choice was correct.</li>
      <li>Open <a href="/upload">Upload</a> and choose the screenshot. You can pick several at once.</li>
      <li>Check the text the site read from it. If the screenshot does not show the result, tap the correct answer.</li>
      <li>Confirm. It is published straight away and anyone can find it.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>No screenshot? Use the “Type it in” tab on the upload page. There are no accounts and nothing to sign up for.</p>

    <h2>Wrong answers</h2>
    <p>
      Answers are crowdsourced, so some will be wrong. Every question page has a “Report a problem” button. When
      uploads disagree about an answer, the question is marked as disputed until it is sorted out.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      There is no login and no tracking profile. To limit abuse the site keeps a salted hash of your IP address next to
      uploads and reports; the address itself is not stored. Screenshots you upload are cropped and published, so do
      not upload anything personal.
    </p>

    <h2>Unofficial fan site</h2>
    <p>
      Cojiro Quiz is a fan project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Nintendo. The Legend of
      Zelda and Ocarina of Time are trademarks of Nintendo. The site uses no official logos or artwork; screenshots are
      contributed by players for reference.
    </p>
    <p>Questions or takedown requests: use the Feedback link at the bottom of any page.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
